The fix for #337 is committed and queued to land on main, but it has not merged yet, so I left the issue open. I queued it at 00:55Z and there was still no verdict at 04:30Z. Main hasn't taken any land since 2026-11-08 13:22Z, so the queue looks stuck or backed up. The manager will still land it after this run ends.

**The fix (commit d161f2e1):**
- **`scripts/release-latest.sh`** prints `true` only when a tag is the newest release of the newest MAJOR.MINOR line. It compares versions as numbers, so 2.10 counts as newer than 2.9, and it ignores pre-releases.
- **The release workflow** (`.github/workflows/release.yml`) fetches all tags first, then publishes with `--latest=<that answer>`. A patch on an older line no longer becomes Latest just because it was published last.
- **Tests** (`scripts/release_latest_test.go`) cover the acceptance case from the issue: a patch on an older line (v2.4.11 after v2.6.1) is not Latest, then a patch on the newest line (v2.6.2) is. They also cover tags pushed in parallel, a newer major, numeric ordering and pre-releases, and check that the workflow uses the script's answer.
- **`docs/VERSIONING.md`** now states the rule.

**Checks:** the new tests pass, and all 16 local `just gates` passed on d161f2e1 (`OVERALL fail=0`).

**Release:**
- **No tag from main.** Main has had a feature (#321) since v2.6.1, and v2.6.2–v2.6.4 already exist on release/2.6, so the patch ships only as backports.
- **Backports:** the backport PRs #457–#463 (release/2.0 to release/2.6) are open, each naming the tag to cut after it merges (v2.0.22 through v2.6.5).
- **Failing check on the backports:** all seven fail one test, `TestCrossTestLegsPruneTheirCargoWorkspace`, because the release branches' `cross-test/trace-carry/run.sh` never cleans up its build workspace. That failure was already on the release branches and is filed as #398; it is not caused by this change.

**Trace check:** this change touches no service handlers. `looper-trace` reports 9 findings, all in cross-test client code that is already filed as #310/#311.

**Left for the next run:** read the land's verdict on the issue, post the outcome comment (commit hash, gates, the gate set the land ran, #398 on the backports), then close #337. My last checkpoint says this.
